  "notes": "Modified cash basis SID with a governmental General Fund and a business-type Utility Fund (water/sewer). Governmental receipts/disbursements from p5, business-type from p7. Governmental roll: 390,010 + 353,414 - 170,320 + 131,957 = 705,061. Business: 287,002 + 528,161 - 394,913 - 131,957 = 288,293 (cash held by county treasurer; statements label it net position; measure recorded as cash). Balance sheet is Statement of Net Position Total column (p1, includes both fund types); 'Cash held at county treasurer' total 945,998 = 657,705 governmental + 288,293 business-type. Payroll and sales tax payable categorized as accrued liabilities. Detail: budget schedule p8 used for revenue lines only (fund 'All funds' since it combines governmental and utility funds; 'Local receipts' budget 540,000 has no actual printed and is omitted); its expenditure lines are superseded by the more detailed p9 functional expenditures by fund column (budget column printed only as a total, not recorded). Sewer column debt services 19,845 split into principal 17,621 and interest 2,224 per p7. Revenue total 881,575 on p8 includes the transfer-free totals of both funds (353,414 + 528,161). Read pages 1-9 of 9 Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p4), Total Governmental Funds column."
